cd ~/k8s-journey/manifests/week3


STEP 1: Deploy a backend that shows its pod name
------------------------------------------------
vi backend.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: backend
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: backend
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: backend
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: echo
        image: hashicorp/http-echo:0.2.3
        args: ["-listen=:8080", "-text=hello from $(POD_NAME)"]
        env:
        - name: POD_NAME
          valueFrom:
            fieldRef:
              fieldPath: metadata.name
        ports:
        - name: http
          containerPort: 8080

k apply -f backend.yaml
k get pods -l app=backend -o wide


STEP 2: Write the Service
-------------------------
vi backend-svc.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: backend
spec:
  selector:
    app: backend
  ports:
  - name: http
    port: 80
    targetPort: http

k apply -f backend-svc.yaml
k get svc backend
k describe svc backend

Note: ClusterIP, Port 80, TargetPort http, Endpoints (3 pod IPs).


STEP 3: EndpointSlices
----------------------
k get endpointslices -l kubernetes.io/service-name=backend
k get endpointslices -l kubernetes.io/service-name=backend -o yaml | grep -E "ip:|addresses|ready"

Compare the IPs with "k get pods -l app=backend -o wide".


STEP 4: Call the Service from a temporary pod
---------------------------------------------
k run tmp --rm -it --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh
  wget -qO- backend          # by name
  wget -qO- backend          # repeat several times: different pods
  for i in $(seq 1 10); do wget -qO- backend; done
  exit

Load balancing across the 3 pods.


STEP 5: Watch endpoints follow the pods
---------------------------------------
Terminal 2:
  k get endpointslices -l kubernetes.io/service-name=backend -w

Terminal 1:
  k scale deploy backend --replicas=5
  k scale deploy backend --replicas=2
  k delete pod -l app=backend

The ClusterIP stays the same the whole time:
  k get svc backend


STEP 6: Selector mistakes (most common Service bug)
---------------------------------------------------
k patch svc backend -p '{"spec":{"selector":{"app":"backendX"}}}'
k get endpointslices -l kubernetes.io/service-name=backend
k describe svc backend | grep Endpoints        # <none>
k run tmp --rm -it --image=busybox:1.36 -- wget -qO- -T 2 backend    # fails

Debug rule: Service not working? First check endpoints. Empty means
the selector doesn't match any READY pod.

Fix:
  k apply -f backend-svc.yaml


STEP 7: ClusterIP is virtual
----------------------------
IP=$(k get svc backend -o jsonpath='{.spec.clusterIP}')
k run tmp --rm -it --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh -c "ping -c 2 -W 1 $IP; wget -qO- $IP"

ping fails (no ICMP rule), wget works (TCP port 80 has a DNAT rule).


STEP 8: Session affinity
------------------------
k patch svc backend -p '{"spec":{"sessionAffinity":"ClientIP"}}'
k run tmp --rm -it --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh -c 'for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do wget -qO- backend; done'
Same pod every time. Remove it:
  k patch svc backend -p '{"spec":{"sessionAffinity":"None"}}'


STEP 9: Headless Service
------------------------
vi backend-headless.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: backend-headless
spec:
  clusterIP: None
  selector:
    app: backend
  ports:
  - port: 8080

k apply -f backend-headless.yaml
k run tmp --rm -it --image=busybox:1.36 -- nslookup backend-headless
k run tmp --rm -it --image=busybox:1.36 -- nslookup backend

Headless returns all pod IPs; normal returns one ClusterIP.


